<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seomjin River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seomjin River is a river in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, about 220 km long, rising in North Jeolla and flowing south into the sea near Gwangyang. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a> its valley was contested between Baekje and the Gaya states, and its lower course gave access to the sea and to trade routes towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seomjin-river.jpg" alt="Seomjin River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Schmidt [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seomjingang_MS3672.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
